      "raw": "Hello friends.\n\nWe all know about [The Hippo](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Hippocalypse), Sentinel Comics's burliest animal-themed, steroid-using nemesis of the Savage Haka.\n![Fig. 1|500x500, 50%](upload://vzKEYywPJMVtBclCmJsgu2zyW6W.jpeg)\n\nYet, it appears that Eddie Wagner is not the only supervillain to go by the moniker of \"The Hippo.\" Coincidentally, it seems that, in 2003, Australian physicist David Morgan-Mar published [a strip](https://www.irregularwebcomic.net/56.html) of his webcomic, *[Irregular Webcomic!](https://www.irregularwebcomic.net/)*,* featuring another supervillain called \"The Hippo.\" Observe:\n![Fig. 2|177x264, 100%](upload://9LNwL91t6PWIiMLYNIVjZg0Xyiu.png)\n\nOther appearances of Morgan-Mar's Hippo include [here](https://www.irregularwebcomic.net/560.html), [here](https://www.irregularwebcomic.net/620.html), and [here](https://www.irregularwebcomic.net/1905.html). His bio and portrait can be found [here](https://www.irregularwebcomic.net/cast/supers.html).\n\nNow, I'm not accusing C&A of stealing anybody's intellectual property. I'm sure this is all just a coincidence. I just thought I should show y'all this.\n\n`*` Tangentially, I highly recommend *Irregular Webcomic* to any webcomic-readers out there. It has content on *many* different topics, including but not limited to LEGOⓇ©™, tabletop RPGs, *Star Wars*, and *Indiana Jones*. See [here](https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Webcomic/IrregularWebcomic) for more information.",
